# p_e5a9 — Mara is a stay-at-home parent (or caregiver); the house is always occupied

Mara is home all day, every day. She may be caring for a young child or elderly parent (whose items aren't catalogued yet, or who is a visitor). The house is active from 7:00 to 22:00. The tablet is used at the kitchen table or coffee table throughout the day. The lunchbox is for a packed lunch eaten at the kitchen table around 12:30. The yoga mat is rolled out on the living room floor for a 20-minute session most mornings (7:30–8:00) before the day's demands begin. The suitcase is for a rare trip (a few times a year). The watering can is used daily at 8:00. The vacuum is used on Saturday mornings.

What sets this apart: on a weekday at 14:00, the tablet is in the house (coffee table or kitchen table), the yoga mat is on the couch (already put away), and the house is occupied. Nothing of Mara's personal items leaves the house on weekdays. The yoga mat is on the floor at 7:45 on weekdays. What would refute it: the tablet or lunchbox found OUT_OF_HOUSE on a weekday, or the yoga mat on the couch at 7:45 on a weekday.

