# p_6e1a — Mara is retired; the house is a slow, predictable rhythm with no work

Mara is retired and home all day, every day. There is no work commute, no school, no gym membership. The day is a gentle rhythm: wake at 7:30, yoga at 8:00, coffee and breakfast at 8:30, gardening/watering at 9:00, a mid-morning walk (10:30–11:30, umbrella if needed), lunch at 12:30, afternoon reading or TV (14:00–17:00), dinner at 18:00, evening TV and bed by 21:30. The tablet is used for email, video calls, and news in the morning and evening. The lunchbox is rarely used (she cooks fresh meals). The suitcase is for an occasional trip to see family (1–2x per year). The watering can is used daily at 9:00. The vacuum is used on Thursday afternoons. The medication bottle is at the bathroom shelf, taken at 8:00 and 20:00.

What sets this apart: on a weekday at 10:45, Mara is out on her walk, so the umbrella may be OUT_OF_HOUSE, the tablet is at the coffee table (left behind), and the house is momentarily empty. At 15:00, the tablet is on the couch or coffee table (afternoon reading/TV). The lunchbox is on the counter for weeks at a time. The yoga mat is on the floor at 8:15 every day. What would refute it: the tablet found OUT_OF_HOUSE, the lunchbox found at the kitchen table at 12:30 (she cooks instead), or the yoga mat on the couch at 8:15.

